  "instance_name": "sharia_law_fearmongering",
  "label": "Fear of Sharia law as a threat to Western values",
  "description": "This is a common trope in Islamophobic discourse that portrays Sharia law as incompatible with Western values and as a threat to freedom, gender equality, or human rights. While Sharia law is a legal system in some Muslim-majority countries, it is often misrepresented or exaggerated in Western media and political discourse. The meme may implicitly reference this fear by using the phrase 'piece of you over here, piece of you over there' to suggest that Muslims are inherently dangerous or incompatible with Western society.",
